@startuml Sequence_Coordinator_Crash_Resume
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

participant Coordinator as "Coordinator\n(separate process)"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"
database Storage as "File Storage (/data/models/)"
participant Gateway as "FastAPI Gateway"
actor Admin as "System / Administrator"

== Regular Execution with State Persistence ==
Note over Coordinator, DB
  Coordinator saves state after EVERY transition:
  - run_id, current round_id, round state
  - latest global model version, path and checksum
end note
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE rounds SET state='AGGREGATING' WHERE round_id=5
Coordinator -> Storage : Write global_model_v6.safetensors (+ SHA-256)
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE rounds SET state='DONE' WHERE round_id=5
Coordinator -> DB : UPDATE runs SET model_version=6
Coordinator -> DB : INSERT round 6, state='OPEN' → 'COLLECTING'

== Unexpected Crash During Round 6 ==
Note over Coordinator : [CRASH: process killed / power failure / OOM]
Note over Gateway, DB
  The gateway is a separate process and keeps running:
  clients can still poll and upload; updates are stored as usual.
end note

== Recovery & Resume ==
Admin -> Coordinator : Restart coordinator process
Coordinator -> DB : SELECT run WHERE state='RUNNING'
DB --> Coordinator : run_id='run-101', model_version=6
Coordinator -> DB : Last round: round_id=6, state='COLLECTING'
Coordinator -> Storage : Verify global_model_v6.safetensors exists & checksum matches
Storage --> Coordinator : OK

alt Round 6 deadline not yet reached
    Coordinator -> Coordinator : Continue round 6 (updates stored during the outage still count)
else Round 6 deadline passed during the outage
    Coordinator -> DB : Apply the normal deadline rule to round 6\n(aggregate if received >= min_participants, else FAILED)
end

Coordinator -> DB : Log event COORDINATOR_RESUMED (run-101, round 6)
Note over Coordinator : The run continues from the last persisted state,\nnot from round 0.
@enduml
